### Why Does This Problem Matter?

Sudoku is the canonical example of constraint satisfaction with backtracking. It demonstrates how to combine constraint checking with exhaustive search. The technique applies to any problem where you must assign values to positions subject to overlapping constraints: scheduling, resource allocation, and configuration validation.

