public class ConstraintSatisfactionPattern {
    // Same pattern applies to:
    // - N-Queens: row, column, diagonal constraints
    // - Graph coloring: adjacent nodes must differ
    // - Scheduling: time slot, room, instructor constraints
}
```

### How Does the Validity Check Work?

The validity check tests three constraints for a digit at position (row, col): the digit must not appear in the same row, the same column, or the same 3x3 box. The box top-left corner is computed as `(row/3)*3` and `(col/3)*3`.

```java
package com.bank.core;

public class ValidityExplained {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        // Box index arithmetic:
        // Cell (4, 7) -> box top-left = (4/3)*3, (7/3)*3 = (3, 6)
        // Cell (1, 2) -> box top-left = (1/3)*3, (2/3)*3 = (0, 0)
        int row = 4, col = 7;
        int boxRow = (row / 3) * 3;  // 3
        int boxCol = (col / 3) * 3;  // 6
        System.out.println("Cell (" + row + "," + col + ") is in box starting at (" + boxRow + "," + boxCol + ")");
    }
}
```

